  <ym-title|Review of a proof unit><label|review-of-a-proof-unit>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: \<langle\>ID and path\<rangle\>

    <item>Role: \<langle\>Lean correspondence / mathematical
    validity\<rangle\>

    <item>Human reviewer: \<langle\>account\<rangle\>

    <item>Agent assistance: \<langle\>tool and role, or none\<rangle\>

    <item>Content SHA-256: \<langle\>output of the fingerprint
    command\<rangle\>

    <item>Manuscript files and labels: \<langle\>check the complete
    manuscript list, including support files\<rangle\>

    <item>Source revision: \<langle\>immutable revision\<rangle\>

    <item>Review task and PR: \<langle\>links\<rangle\>

    <item>Outcome: \<langle\>changes requested / accepted locally,
    conditional on stated dependencies\<rangle\>
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Findings and evidence><label|findings-and-evidence>

  \<langle\>Check the appropriate questions in docs/proof-standard.md. Cite
  exact steps, declarations, definitions, hypotheses, and any commands
  actually run. For mathematical review, verify the detail of the proofs and
  the actual statements and applicability of literature results. Identify
  useful existing results that avoid unnecessary rederivation, and any gap
  hidden by an appeal to a supposedly standard fact.\<rangle\>

  <section|Required changes and remaining
  uncertainty><label|required-changes-and-remaining-uncertainty>

  \<langle\>Actionable findings, dependency caveats, and anything this review
  did not check.\<rangle\>

  <section|Acceptance><label|acceptance>

  \<langle\>The responsible human reviewer records acceptance only after
  required changes are resolved. A new content fingerprint requires renewed
  acceptance.\<rangle\>
</body>

